maemo-statusmenu-volume (1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New tuning format: x-maemo.volume.tuning and .incall, ascending centibels
  * Ladders come from wireplumber, N900 tables are the fallback
  * In-call ladder is picked from phone-role sink inputs, not MCE call_state
  * In-call volume is now actually written to the sink
  * Call stream is driven directly, media and VOIP volumes are independent
  * Track the current sink's channel count instead of the first one seen
  * Own the MCE key and display match rules instead of relying on the host
  * Ignore an idle mm_key rather than reading it as volume-up
  * Fix crash paths on NULL proplist key and ladders shorter than two steps
  * Drop the unused GConf dependency

 -- Ivaylo Dimitrov <ivo.g.dimitrov.75@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:39:31 +0300

